---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout title="Signal Locked" description="You found it. The hidden room behind the portfolio.">
  <section class="py-16">
    <p class="mb-4 font-mono text-sm text-star-green">SIGNAL LOCKED // COORDINATES VERIFIED</p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold text-nebula-50 md:text-5xl">The Observatory</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-nebula-400">
      You found it. This is the room behind the portfolio. The dev commentary track.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl space-y-8 pb-16">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-nebula-700/50 bg-nebula-900/50 p-6">
      <h2 class="mb-4 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nebula-100">Why This Exists</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-nebula-400">
        <p>
          I wanted to build a portfolio that wasn't just a portfolio. Most portfolio sites
          are static showcases. You scroll. You read. You leave. I wanted something where
          the act of exploring the site was itself a kind of project.
        </p>
        <p>
          So I built two layers. The surface is clean and professional. It does the job.
          The hidden layer is where the real experiments live. Stars you can click. Games
          hidden in words. A terminal with secrets. A 22-minute time loop that subtly
          shifts the atmosphere.
        </p>
        <p>
          The idea came from Outer Wilds. That game uses a 22-minute loop as a core mechanic.
          Everything resets, but your knowledge persists. I wanted the same feeling here.
          Your discoveries are permanent. The site remembers you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-xl border border-nebula-700/50 bg-nebula-900/50 p-6">
      <h2 class="mb-4 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nebula-100">The Stack</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-nebula-400">
        <p>
          Astro handles the static shell. Svelte islands bring interactivity where it's needed.
          Three.js renders the starfield. LittleJS powers the mini-games at under 7KB.
          Tone.js generates ambient music. Matter.js makes text explode when you click it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything heavy loads dynamically. The initial bundle stays under 200KB. Lighthouse
          score stays above 90. The fancy stuff happens in the background, after the page
          is already readable.
        </p>
        <p>
          All state lives in localStorage. No accounts. No server. No tracking. Just a
          key-value store that remembers what you found.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-xl border border-nebula-700/50 bg-nebula-900/50 p-6">
      <h2 class="mb-4 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-nebula-100">The Numbers</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-lg bg-nebula-800/50 p-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-star-blue" id="stat-discoveries">0</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-nebula-500">Possible Discoveries</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg bg-nebula-800/50 p-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-star-gold">4</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-nebula-500">Hidden Games</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg bg-nebula-800/50 p-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-star-pink">3</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-nebula-500">Constellations</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg bg-nebula-800/50 p-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold text-star-green">22</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-nebula-500">Minute Loop</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-xl border border-star-gold/20 bg-star-gold/5 p-6">
      <h2 class="mb-4 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-star-gold/90">A Secret for the Secret Finders</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-star-gold/60">
        You got here through the terminal. You scanned the page, found the frequency,
        and followed the coordinates. That takes curiosity. If you're building something
        and want to add hidden layers like these, reach out. I love talking about
        this stuff.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<script>
  // Record the observatory discovery
  try {
    const raw = localStorage.getItem('observatory:state');
    if (raw) {
      const state = JSON.parse(raw);
      if (!state.discoveries.includes('meta:observatory-found')) {
        state.discoveries.push('meta:observatory-found');
        localStorage.setItem('observatory:state', JSON.stringify(state));
        window.dispatchEvent(
          new CustomEvent('observatory:discovery', {
            detail: { id: 'meta:observatory-found', category: 'meta', label: 'Found the Observatory' },
          })
        );
      }
    }
  } catch {
    // ignore
  }

  // Show total discovery count from knowledge graph
  const statEl = document.getElementById('stat-discoveries');
  if (statEl) {
    // Hard-coded count that matches the knowledge graph nodes
    statEl.textContent = '35+';
  }
</script>
